title: $:/plugins/tw-enc-sync/readme

! Encrypted per-tiddler sync

Every tiddler is stored as an opaque AES-256-GCM encrypted file; only the manifest and the tiddlers you open are loaded. ''Save'' (Ctrl+S or the save button) writes pending changes to every ''save target''; the second page-control button ''Publish to GitHub now'' makes the GitHub repository match this wiki whatever the targets are (it also seeds an empty repository from your local files).

!! Save targets

`$:/config/ext/enc/SaveTarget` is a comma list of `github`, `folder`, `zip` (spaces are fine, unknown words are ignored; it can be changed in the app). Default: opened from `file:` -> `folder` (`zip` if the browser has no File System Access API), opened from `http(s)` -> `github`.

* `github`: one commit via the Git Data API, a few seconds after you stop editing and on Save. Token as before (Control Panel > Saving > GitHub), kept in ''sessionStorage'' (this tab) instead of `localStorage`; change with `$:/config/ext/enc/TokenStorage` = `memory` or `local`. Use a fine-grained token limited to this one repository: Contents read and write, Metadata read.
* `folder`: writes the changed encrypted files and the new manifest straight into the wiki folder (the one that contains `tw.html`). The first Save asks you to pick it once; the permission is remembered. Files first, manifest last. The timer only writes here if the permission is already granted, it never opens a dialog.
* `zip`: Save downloads `tw-update-<counter>.zip` (changed files, the new manifest, and `_remove.txt` with paths to delete); unzip it over the wiki folder and delete the files listed in `_remove.txt`. Only on Save, never from the timer.

<$list filter="[[$:/temp/ext/enc/status]is[tiddler]]">Targets: <code><$view tiddler="$:/temp/ext/enc/status" field="targets"/></code> -- unsaved local changes: <b><$view tiddler="$:/temp/ext/enc/status" field="unsaved-local"/></b>, not yet published to GitHub: <b><$view tiddler="$:/temp/ext/enc/status" field="unpublished"/></b></$list>

For safety, raw HTML that could run script in this page is neutered: `srcdoc` attributes and `javascript:` URLs are dropped, `base`/`meta`/`link` elements are inert, and messages from other windows are ignored. Create `$:/config/ext/enc/AllowActiveHtml` with the text `yes` to switch the element filter off (only if you trust every tiddler). Tiddler titles are kept out of the browser console unless `$:/config/ext/enc/ConsoleLog` is `yes`.

<$list filter="[[$:/temp/ext/enc/status]is[tiddler]]">Status: <code><$text text={{$:/temp/ext/enc/status}}/></code></$list>
